      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While elevation is good for reducing swelling, relying solely on ibuprofen for a potentially concerning symptom isn't ideal, especially when you're unsure. Since your surgeon is unavailable, try applying a cold pack wrapped in a towel to the area for 15-20 minutes at a time. If the warmth becomes intense, you notice redness spreading, or you feel any sharp pain, you should consider going to urgent care instead of waiting until Monday.",
